abstract: "Dot-Trace Theory proposes that persistent, socially accessible interaction traces mediate the co-evolution of agent behavior, memory structure, and social topology. This repository contains the foundation manuscript, reproducible synthetic experiment scaffolding, reference simulators, validation runners, and documentation."
